Links open in Brave, not in whatever the desktop picked
=====================================================

`/__eipc__/open-external` handed every URL to `xdg-open`, which means the browser you got depended on
the desktop's default — and on this machine that is not the one the agent tooling can drive.

The launcher now resolves a browser itself, first match wins:

    $QUIXI_BROWSER, brave-browser, brave, brave-bin, chromium,
    google-chrome-stable, google-chrome, then xdg-open

Brave is first because it is what this edition targets and it exposes CDP, which is what the
browser-driving skill needs. Chromium-family next, since the same driver works. `xdg-open` stays as the
last resort so an unfamiliar desktop still opens something.

A small `which()` walks PATH — this crate does not otherwise depend on a lookup crate, and adding one
for seven candidates would be silly.
